# Women's Life Stages

## Philosophy

Women's health requirements change with age, hormonal status, reproductive stage and lifestyle.

The AI must always personalize recommendations according to the woman's life stage rather than using a one-size-fits-all approach.

---

# Stage 1 — Adolescence (13–19 Years)

Primary Focus

- Healthy growth
- Nutrition
- Iron deficiency
- Menstrual health
- PCOS awareness
- Vitamin deficiencies
- Lifestyle counselling

Educational Topics

- First menstrual cycle
- Healthy eating
- Exercise
- Acne & hormones
- Importance of haemoglobin

---

# Stage 2 — Young Women (20–30 Years)

Focus

- PCOS
- Thyroid
- Fertility awareness
- Vitamin deficiencies
- Lifestyle diseases
- Weight management
- Sexual & reproductive health

---

# Stage 3 — Newly Married / Pregnancy Planning

Focus

- Preconception screening
- Blood group
- Thyroid
- Vitamin D
- Vitamin B12
- Rubella immunity
- General wellness
- Genetic counselling (where appropriate)

---

# Stage 4 — Pregnancy

Focus

- Prenatal diagnostics
- Gestational diabetes
- Thyroid monitoring
- Anaemia
- Nutritional monitoring
- Infection screening

---

# Stage 5 — Motherhood

Focus

- Postpartum recovery
- Iron
- Vitamin D
- Lactation support
- Hormonal recovery
- Mental wellbeing awareness

---

# Stage 6 — Women 40+

Focus

- Diabetes
- Heart health
- Bone health
- Breast health
- Cervical screening
- Preventive health packages

---

# Stage 7 — Menopause

Focus

- Bone density
- Vitamin D
- Hormonal balance
- Heart disease
- Healthy ageing
- Preventive diagnostics

---

Golden Rule

Every recommendation must be appropriate to the woman's life stage.
